PERF-VEC-QRY-003-RC08	PERF-VEC-QRY-003	Thread pool exhaustion from concurrent probing	thread-pool-exhaustion-from-concurrent-probing	High `nprobe` + high concurrency causes thread pool saturation; queries queue waiting for available compute threads.	\N	{chromadb,milvus,qdrant,weaviate}	{"milvus": "`nlist` and `nprobe` parameters directly tunable. Milvus sizing tool recommends `nlist = 4 * sqrt(n)`. High `nprobe` should trigger alerts; tune downward via metrics `query.ivf_probe_efficiency`. Milvus 2.4+ has query node scaling to distribute IVF probe load.", "qdrant": "Uses HNSW by default, not IVF. IVF available in FAISS integration; parameters accessible via collection config. Qdrant recommends HNSW for most use cases; IVF only for extreme scale with tight latency budget.", "chromadb": "IVF exposed via FAISS backend (if configured). `nlist` and `nprobe` tunable via Chroma client API. Default values conservative; increasing both together risks CPU exhaustion.", "weaviate": "HNSW primary algorithm; IVF not natively supported. Custom index types possible via plugins, but not recommended. Tuning via HNSW `m` and `ef_construct` instead.", "postgresql": "IVFFlat index exposes `lists` (equivalent to nlist) at index creation time and `ivfflat.probes` (equivalent to nprobe) at query time. Default `probes=1` conservative; set via `SET ivfflat.probes = X` per connection. Formula `lists = 4 * sqrt(n)` recommended."}	\N	2026-02-23 20:18:30.6388	2026-02-23 20:18:30.638801
