HLTH-VEC-RES-001-RC15	HLTH-VEC-RES-001	Organization-/account-level caps	organization-account-level-caps	SaaS vendors apply org-level caps (projects, collections, indices) that are hit even if per-project limits appear free in the UI. Vendor-Specific Notes: - Pinecone: Database and index limits by plan; collections/namespaces count against project quotas; org-level project limits also apply. - Milvus: Collection and partition counts controlled by `maxGeneralCapacity` and explicit collection/partition limits; backed by etcd key quotas. - Qdrant: No fixed hard collection limit, but collection and shard counts are constrained by RAM/disk and cluster coordination overhead. - Weaviate: Per-instance collection/class limits and multi-tenancy design strongly affect how many “collections” are feasible. - pgvector: PostgreSQL relation limits are huge, but practical limits come from catalog size, autovacuum overhead, and connection usage. - MongoDB Atlas Vector Search: Each vector index per collection counts toward cluster index limits and shard capacity. - Elasticsearch/OpenSearch: Index and shard-count limits (`cluster.max_shards_per_node`) and cluster-state size determine how many vector indices can exist. - Redis VSS: Logical “collections” are modeled via keys/prefixes; practical limits derive from memory, key count, and RDB/AOF file sizes rather than a hard collection cap.	\N	{chromadb,milvus,qdrant,weaviate}	null	\N	2026-02-23 20:18:30.639156	2026-02-23 20:18:30.639157
