SEC-SQL-PAT-002-RC15	SEC-SQL-PAT-002	Patch delivery and content distribution delays	patch-delivery-and-content-distribution-delays	Regional patch delivery networks or vendor infrastructure limitations delay patch availability in certain geographic locations or cloud regions. **Organizational Root Causes:** - **Reactive patching culture driven by compliance audits** – Organizations only prioritize patches when audits or regulatory reviews demand them, missing the actual threat window before patches are deployed. - **Absence of formal SLAs for critical patch deployment** – No defined targets (e.g., "critical patches within 48 hours") create ambiguity about urgency and accountability. - **Organizational unwillingness to accept short-term operational disruption** – Leadership resists scheduled maintenance windows that would provide time for testing and deployment, prioritizing uptime over security. - **Insufficient staffing and training** – Database teams lack expertise in patch management procedures, patch testing, and incident recovery, slowing deployment and increasing fear of failure. - **Siloed security and operations teams** – Security teams identify vulnerabilities but operations teams deploy patches; lack of coordination and shared accountability leads to delays and miscommunication. - **Lack of automation investment** – Organizations with manual, spreadsheet-based patch tracking and deployment processes cannot scale to modern vulnerability volumes and disclosure timelines. - **Poor patch communication from vendor relationships** – Organizations lack early access to security advisories, advance notification of critical patches, or vendor escalation channels for urgent issues. - **Technical debt preventing safe patching** – Legacy database configurations, undocumented customizations, or fragile application dependencies make patch testing and deployment extremely risky. - **Competing priorities with limited budgets** – Organizations allocate resources to new features and business initiatives rather than security maintenance, leaving patching perpetually underfunded. - **Inadequate incident response and disaster recovery preparedness** – Lack of confidence in rollback and recovery procedures increases organizational risk aversion to patching.	\N	{mariadb,oracle,postgresql,vertica}	null	\N	2026-02-23 20:18:30.639889	2026-02-23 20:18:30.639889
